66Q326 666 387 610T449 465Q449 422 429 383T381 315T301 241Q265 210 201 149L142 93L218 92Q375 92 385 97Q392 99 409 186V189H449V186Q448 183 436 95T421 3V0H50V19V31Q50 38 56 46T86 81Q115 113 136 137Q145 147 170 174T204 211T233 244T261 278T284 308T305 340T320 369T333 401T340 431T343 464Q343 527 309 573T212 619Q179 619 154 602T119 569T109 550Q109 549 114 549Q132 549 151 535T170 489Q170 464 154 447T109 429Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-32\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> pairs of parallel congruent sides.</p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's examine each of the given polygons.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.899ex\" height=\"2.343ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.505ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 817.5 1008.6\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-4-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-4-Title\">\\mathcal{Q}</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJCAL-51\" d=\"M114 286Q114 358 151 433T249 569T392 667T558 705Q653 705 713 641T774 460Q774 389 750 322T687 206T600 114T504 46T412 4L399 -2Q542 -62 636 -62Q660 -62 670 -54T686 -27T700 0Q734 34 770 34Q787 34 787 23Q787 -18 720 -74T563 -131Q485 -131 350 -83T145 -34Q127 -34 127 -22Q127 -12 144 5T190 31L200 34L237 35Q386 38 467 79Q550 120 612 210T675 416Q675 510 625 573T484 636Q410 636 346 587T248 469T214 333Q214 306 221 281T243 229T288 188T360 172Q403 172 441 188T490 205Q510 205 510 192Q505 162 432 132T287 102Q206 102 160 155T114 286Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJCAL-51\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> is <em>not</em> similar to <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://